---
layout: base.njk
title: Matt Hovis
permalink: /
charts: true
---
{%- set months = { "01": "Jan", "02": "Feb", "03": "Mar", "04": "Apr", "05": "May", "06": "Jun", "07": "Jul", "08": "Aug", "09": "Sep", "10": "Oct", "11": "Nov", "12": "Dec" } -%}

<section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-h">
  <div class="wrap hero__grid">
    <div class="hero__main">
      <p class="designation">
        <span class="designation__code">MH-26</span>
        <span>Developer / Business analyst</span>
        <span class="designation__loc">Atlanta, GA</span>
      </p>
      <div class="hero__id">
        <figure class="portrait">
          <img src="/matt-hovis.jpg?v=2" alt="Matt Hovis" width="640" height="640" fetchpriority="high" />
        </figure>
        <h1 class="hero__title" id="hero-h">Matt Hovis</h1>
      </div>
      <p class="hero__sub">I love taking an idea and turning it into something people use.</p>
      <p class="lede">
        For four years I turned what clients needed into work a developer could pick up and build.
        Now I build it myself.
      </p>
      <div class="cta">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="#story">My story</a>
        <a class="btn" href="#work">Case files</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero__fig">
      {% include "schematic.njk" %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--alt" id="story" aria-labelledby="story-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="sec-head">
      <p class="sec-head__tag"><span class="sec-head__num">01</span>Origin</p>
      <h2 id="story-h">How I got here</h2>
    </header>
    <ol class="story">
      <li class="chapter">
        <p class="chapter__mark"><span class="chapter__year">2022</span><span class="chapter__label">Support desk</span></p>
        <p>I started on the support desk of a company whose software runs repair shops. I learned the product by fixing what broke for the people using it, and I learned SQL to find out why it broke.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="chapter">
        <p class="chapter__mark"><span class="chapter__year">2023</span><span class="chapter__label">Business analyst</span></p>
        <p>I moved into business analysis. I wrote the requirements, tested the releases, and was on the call for launches in Canada, France, and Japan. I knew what needed to be built and why. Other people built it.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="chapter">
        <p class="chapter__mark"><span class="chapter__year">2026</span><span class="chapter__label">The team</span></p>
        <p>Then I got the chance to form a team with people who have decades of experience building apps. I jumped. Through a lot of collaboration, learning, and hard work, with AI coding agents beside me, I went from my first commit in February to <strong>1,192 merged pull requests</strong> by November.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="chapter chapter--now">
        <p class="chapter__mark"><span class="chapter__year">Now</span><span class="chapter__label">Builder</span></p>
        <p>I still start where I always have: with the person who has the problem. The difference is that now I build the fix. I can confidently say I build apps.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <section class="spec" aria-labelledby="spec-h">
      <header class="spec__head">
        <h2 id="spec-h">The numbers so far</h2>
        <span>Unit MH-26 · as of 12 Nov 2026</span>
      </header>
      <dl class="spec__gauges">
        <div class="gauge"><dt>Pull requests merged</dt><dd>1,192</dd><p>of 1,395 opened</p></div>
        <div class="gauge"><dt>Lines merged</dt><dd>660k</dd><p>+660,728 / −103,946</p></div>
        <div class="gauge"><dt>Test code</dt><dd>124k</dd><p>lines in 1,347 files</p></div>
        <div class="gauge"><dt>Median open → merge</dt><dd>2.6<small>h</small></dd><p>main product repository</p></div>
      </dl>
      <dl class="spec__rows">
        <div><dt>Repositories</dt><dd>13 with merged work, across work, collaborations, and personal</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Primary stack</dt><dd>PHP · Laravel · Vue · TypeScript · Swift · SQL</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Tooling</dt><dd>Claude Code · GitHub · Jira · Confluence</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Prior role</dt><dd>Business analyst: client needs into buildable work</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Certifications</dt><dd>SQL · Atlassian Jira and Confluence</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </section>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="work" aria-labelledby="work-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="sec-head">
      <p class="sec-head__tag"><span class="sec-head__num">02</span>Case files</p>
      <h2 id="work-h">Selected work</h2>
      <p class="sec-head__intro">2026, on a repair and service-management platform for retail chains. Client names are left out.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="cases">
      {% for c in work %}
      <article class="case panel">
        <header class="case__bar">
          <span class="case__id">CF-{{ "0" if loop.index < 10 }}{{ loop.index }}</span>
          <span class="case__tag">{{ c.tag }}</span>
          <span class="case__when">{{ c.when }}</span>
        </header>
        <h3 class="case__title">{{ c.title }}</h3>
        <dl class="case__body">
          <dt>Problem</dt><dd>{{ c.problem }}</dd>
          <dt>Action</dt><dd>{{ c.did }}</dd>
          <dt>Result</dt><dd class="case__result">{{ c.result }}</dd>
        </dl>
        <ul class="chips" aria-label="Stack">{% for s in c.stack %}<li>{{ s }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
      </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--alt" id="code" aria-labelledby="code-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="sec-head">
      <p class="sec-head__tag"><span class="sec-head__num">03</span>Telemetry</p>
      <h2 id="code-h">2026 in code</h2>
      <p class="sec-head__intro">From GitHub.</p>
    </header>

    <figure class="chart panel" id="heatmap-fig">
      <figcaption class="chart__cap">
        <span class="chart__no">Fig. 2</span>
        <h3>Contributions per day</h3>
        <p>Commits, pull requests, and reviews. 3,263 in 2026, on 192 days.</p>
      </figcaption>
      <div class="chart__scroll"><div class="chart__plot" id="heatmap" role="img" aria-label="Calendar heatmap of GitHub contributions per day in 2026. Activity starts in February and peaks at 282 on 16 September."></div></div>
      <div class="heat-legend" aria-hidden="true">
        <span>Less</span><i class="h0"></i><i class="h1"></i><i class="h2"></i><i class="h3"></i><i class="h4"></i><span>More</span>
      </div>
      <details class="table-view">
        <summary>Show as table</summary>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Month</th><th scope="col">Contributions</th><th scope="col">Active days</th><th scope="col">Busiest day</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {% for m in contribMonths %}<tr><th scope="row">{{ m.month }}</th><td>{{ m.total }}</td><td>{{ m.activeDays }}</td><td>{{ m.peak }}</td></tr>
            {% endfor %}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </details>
    </figure>

    <div class="chart-row">
      <figure class="chart panel" id="months-fig">
        <figcaption class="chart__cap">
          <span class="chart__no">Fig. 3</span>
          <h3>Pull requests opened per month</h3>
          <p>By where the work lives.</p>
        </figcaption>
        <ul class="legend" aria-label="Legend">
          <li><i class="sw sw--1"></i>Day job</li>
          <li><i class="sw sw--2"></i>Collaborations</li>
          <li><i class="sw sw--3"></i>Personal</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="chart__plot" id="months" role="img" aria-label="Stacked bar chart of pull requests opened per month, February to November 2026. Peak in July with 442."></div>
        <details class="table-view">
          <summary>Show as table</summary>
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Month</th><th scope="col">Day job</th><th scope="col">Collaborations</th><th scope="col">Personal</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              {% for m, v in stats.prsByMonth %}
              <tr><th scope="row">{{ months[m.slice(5)] }}</th><td>{{ v.work or 0 }}</td><td>{{ v.collab or 0 }}</td><td>{{ v.personal or 0 }}</td></tr>
              {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </details>
      </figure>

      <figure class="chart panel" id="langs-fig">
        <figcaption class="chart__cap">
          <span class="chart__no">Fig. 4</span>
          <h3>Lines added by language</h3>
          <p>Merged pull requests, code files only. A minimum: counts read the first 100 files of each PR.</p>
        </figcaption>
        <div class="chart__plot" id="langs" role="img" aria-label="Bar chart of lines added by language. PHP leads with about 281 thousand, then JavaScript, Swift, Vue, TypeScript, Kotlin, HTML, and CSS."></div>
        <details class="table-view">
          <summary>Show as table</summary>
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Language</th><th scope="col">Lines added</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>{% for l in stats.languages %}<tr><th scope="row">{{ l[0] }}</th><td>{{ l[1] }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
          </table>
        </details>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <ul class="readouts">
      <li><span class="readouts__k">Streak</span><strong>19 days</strong><span>in a row with a merged PR, 29 Jun – 17 Jul</span></li>
      <li><span class="readouts__k">Peak day</span><strong>83 merges</strong><span>on 17 September</span></li>
      <li><span class="readouts__k">Tickets</span><strong>417</strong><span>named in PR titles on the main product</span></li>
      <li><span class="readouts__k">Commits</span><strong>3,582</strong><span>across 11,821 changed files</span></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <script type="application/json" id="stats-data">{{ stats | dump | safe }}</script>
</section>

<section class="section" id="projects" aria-labelledby="projects-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="sec-head">
      <p class="sec-head__tag"><span class="sec-head__num">04</span>Hangar</p>
      <h2 id="projects-h">Side projects</h2>
    </header>
    <div class="projects">
      {% for p in projects %}
      <article class="project panel{% if p.featured %} project--featured{% endif %}">
        <p class="project__bar"><span>Unit {{ "0" if loop.index < 10 }}{{ loop.index }}</span><span>{{ p.kind }}</span></p>
        <h3>{{ p.name }}</h3>
        <p class="project__blurb">{{ p.blurb }}</p>
        <ul class="chips" aria-label="Stack">{% for s in p.stack %}<li>{{ s }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
        {% if p.links.length %}
        <p class="project__links">{% for l in p.links %}<a href="{{ l.href }}"{% if l.href.startsWith('http') %} rel="noopener"{% endif %}>{{ l.label }} <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>{% endfor %}</p>
        {% endif %}
      </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--alt" id="career" aria-labelledby="career-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="sec-head">
      <p class="sec-head__tag"><span class="sec-head__num">05</span>Service record</p>
      <h2 id="career-h">Career</h2>
    </header>
    <ol class="record">
      {% for j in career %}
      <li class="record__item{% if loop.first %} is-current{% endif %}">
        <p class="record__rev">Rev {{ "0" if (career.length - loop.index0) < 10 }}{{ career.length - loop.index0 }}</p>
        <p class="record__when">{{ j.when }}</p>
        <div class="record__body">
          <h3>{{ j.role }}</h3>
          <p class="record__org">{{ j.org }}</p>
          <p>{{ j.body }}</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
    <div class="creds">
      <h3>Certifications and study</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>SQL certificate, 2022</li>
        <li>Atlassian: Jira Service Management, Jira, and Confluence fundamentals</li>
        <li>Working toward a Bachelor of Applied Science</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-h">
  <div class="wrap about">
    <div>
      <header class="sec-head">
        <p class="sec-head__tag"><span class="sec-head__num">06</span>Operator</p>
        <h2 id="about-h">Outside work</h2>
      </header>
      <ul class="interests">
        <li>Video games</li>
        <li>Comics and manga</li>
        <li>Gunpla</li>
        <li>Atlanta Braves</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <figure class="photo">
      <div class="photo__frame">
        <img src="/gunpla-sm.jpg" alt="A finished white, blue, and red model kit standing next to a tabby cat" loading="lazy" width="900" height="1200" />
      </div>
      <figcaption><span class="chart__no">Fig. 5</span> A finished kit, and one of my cats.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

